The rule for k_recovery says it returns the object recovered from the reply, as canonical JSON text, or NO_OBJECT. The cell fence[ A S ] contains a fence with two parts: A and S. The last object inside a code fence is S, so k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of S. The rewritten text fence[ A S ] A adds A after the fence, so the last object inside a code fence is A, and k_recovery returns the canonical JSON of A. Since A and S are different objects, the answer moves.